 msgid "For experts, and for a 2.35:1 or 2.39:1 screen or films that change shape from scene to scene (IMAX scenes). Off (the default): Dolby Vision videos are shown as always. On, with the view mode Normal: each scene of a Dolby Vision video is enlarged so that its picture, without the black bars that its Dolby Vision data mark (level 5), fills as much of the screen as it can, and follows the film when its shape changes. Nothing of the picture is cut off: a scene taller than the screen fills its height, with bars at the sides. The screen is the area set in Settings > System > Display > Video calibration: for a 2.35:1 or 2.39:1 screen, move its top and bottom edges there. Videos without that data, and any other view mode you choose, are shown as before. Subtitles stay on the screen. Applies at once."
